PREFACE

  No. 5 of 2011

  Legislation (Amendment) Act, 2011

  An Act to amend the Legislation Act, 1992, so as to shorten the period within which the official text must be made current, to remove the power to defer publication, and for connected purposes.

PREAMBLE

  BE IT ENACTED by the Assembly of Atlantis, and by the authority of the same, as follows:

BODY

SECTION 1 - Short title

  This Act may be cited as the Legislation (Amendment) Act, 2011, and shall be read as one with the Legislation Act, 1992 (in this Act referred to as "the principal Act").

SECTION 2 - Amendment of section 5

  In section 5 of the principal Act, for the words "thirty days" there shall be substituted the words "seven days".

SECTION 3 - Repeal of power to defer publication

  Section 11 of the principal Act is repealed.

SECTION 4 - Consequential amendment of section 13

  In section 13(1) of the principal Act, the words "other than a decision to defer publication under section 11," are repealed.

SECTION 5 - Commencement

  This Act shall come into operation on the first day of January, 2012.
